@param \Discord\Parts\Guild\Guild|string $guild The guild or its id.
@param array $queryparams Query string params to add to the request, at least one (no validation).
@see \Discord\Repository\Guild\MessageRepository::freshen() for the query parameters.
@return \React\Promise\PromiseInterface<\Discord\Parts\Guild\Member\GuildSearch>
@since 10.67.0

discord\\oauth2\\session::setcommandperm.documentation:
Sets who can use one of an application's commands in a guild, replacing the permissions it had there.
Discord only accepts this with a user's token that has the `applications.commands.permissions.update`
scope, never a bot's. The user needs the manage_guild and manage_roles permissions in the guild, and
must be able to use the command themselves.
@link https://docs.discord.com/developers/interactions/application-commands#edit-application-command-permissions
@param \Discord\Parts\Guild\Guild|string $guild The guild.
@param \Discord\Parts\Application\Command\Command|string $command The command or its ID; the application's ID sets the default for all its commands.
@param (\Discord\Parts\Application\Command\Permission|array)[] $permissions At most 100, each with `id`, `type` and `permission`.
@param \Discord\Parts\Application\Application|string|null $application The application or its id; the bot's own if omitted.
@return \React\Promise\PromiseInterface<\Discord\Parts\Application\Command\CommandPermissions>
@since 10.60.0

